{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Torsion Module.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Torsion Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"torsion module torsion module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Torsion Module.md","fileName":"Torsion Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Torsion Module","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:05\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Associated Primes and Module Dimension]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Associated Primes and Module Dimension","Associated Prime","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Torsion Module.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Torsion Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"torsion module torsion module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Torsion Module.md","fileName":"Torsion Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Torsion Module","heading":"Torsion Module","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A torsion module over an integral domain is a module in which every element is annihilated by some nonzero scalar. In the source's broader formulation, the annihilating scalar is required to be a non-zero-divisor.\n\nOver a Noetherian integral domain, M is torsion exactly when the zero ideal is not an [[Associated Prime]]. Torsion records elements supported away from the generic prime.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Associated Primes and Module Dimension","Associated Prime","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Torsion Module.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Torsion Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"torsion module torsion module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Torsion Module.md","fileName":"Torsion Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Torsion Module","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[commutativealgebra.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Associated Primes and Module Dimension","Associated Prime","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}